1
00:00:00,580 --> 00:00:01,060
Welcome back!

2
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:03,800
Last time we finished Level Five.

3
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:08,700
You learned six spelling rules, and you learned them all.

4
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:13,300
Today we are starting Level Six, and this one is different.

5
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:16,460
Today you are not learning a rule.

6
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:23,480
Today you are learning a trick — a trick that lets you read a whole pile of words at once.

7
00:00:24,640 --> 00:00:26,080
Let me show you what I mean.

8
00:00:26,940 --> 00:00:27,840
Here is a word.

9
00:00:28,460 --> 00:00:28,760
Cat.

10
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:34,190
Now watch what happens when I change just ONE letter.

11
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:35,100
The first one.

12
00:00:36,580 --> 00:00:36,940
Cat...

13
00:00:38,340 --> 00:00:38,480
bat.

14
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:40,600
Did you see that?

15
00:00:41,240 --> 00:00:43,240
Everything else stayed the same.

16
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:47,760
Only the front changed, and it made a brand new word.

17
00:00:48,480 --> 00:00:49,600
That is the trick.

18
00:00:50,480 --> 00:00:54,240
And once you know it, you can read hundreds of words.

19
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:56,880
Look at the end of the word.

20
00:00:58,570 --> 00:00:59,520
C-A-T.

21
00:01:00,360 --> 00:01:03,520
The last two letters are a and t.

22
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:05,820
Say that ending with me.

23
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:07,040
At.

24
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:09,980
Now here is the important part.

25
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:14,900
Every word that ends in those two letters says At.

26
00:01:15,980 --> 00:01:22,360
So all I have to do is put a different letter in front, and I get another word I can read.

27
00:01:23,240 --> 00:01:23,540
Watch.

28
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:27,420
I will keep At and change only the front.

29
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:28,860
Cat.

30
00:01:29,660 --> 00:01:30,080
Bat.

31
00:01:31,060 --> 00:01:31,300
Hat.

32
00:01:32,520 --> 00:01:32,900
Rat.

33
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:34,260
Mat.

34
00:01:35,660 --> 00:01:36,080
Sat.

35
00:01:37,060 --> 00:01:37,440
Pat.

36
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:38,820
Fat.

37
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:41,100
Eight words.

38
00:01:41,720 --> 00:01:44,260
And you only had to learn one ending.

39
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:47,480
That is called a word family.

40
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:53,780
All those words are in the At family, because they all end the same way.

41
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:56,480
You just read eight words.

42
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:57,780
Well done!

43
00:01:59,040 --> 00:02:01,940
Let's keep the same vowel and change the ending.

44
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:04,020
Here is our next family.

45
00:02:04,920 --> 00:02:05,500
An.

46
00:02:06,380 --> 00:02:07,560
Listen to the vowel.

47
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:11,060
It is still a short a, just like At.

48
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:13,840
Only the last letter changed.

49
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:15,700
Can.

50
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:17,280
Man.

51
00:02:18,340 --> 00:02:18,980
Fan.

52
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:20,540
Ran.

53
00:02:21,440 --> 00:02:22,180
Pan.

54
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:23,780
Tan.

55
00:02:24,680 --> 00:02:25,340
Van.

56
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:26,900
Ban.

57
00:02:28,080 --> 00:02:28,740
Eight more.

58
00:02:29,740 --> 00:02:32,040
That is sixteen words already.

59
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:34,840
And one more a family.

60
00:02:35,860 --> 00:02:36,100
Ap.

61
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:37,580
Cap.

62
00:02:38,800 --> 00:02:39,200
Map.

63
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:40,740
Nap.

64
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:42,300
Tap.

65
00:02:43,420 --> 00:02:43,880
Lap.

66
00:02:45,120 --> 00:02:45,440
Gap.

67
00:02:46,740 --> 00:02:48,370
Look at what is happening.

68
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:51,620
The a stays put every single time.

69
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:54,940
It is only the letters around it that move.

70
00:02:55,780 --> 00:02:57,720
You are doing really well.

71
00:02:58,920 --> 00:03:00,400
Now we change the vowel.

72
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:03,200
This time it is a short e.

73
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:05,980
Our family is En.

74
00:03:06,980 --> 00:03:07,640
Hen.

75
00:03:08,780 --> 00:03:09,200
Ten.

76
00:03:10,220 --> 00:03:10,860
Pen.

77
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:12,720
Men.

78
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:14,420
Den.

79
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:16,740
Say the ending with me.

80
00:03:17,420 --> 00:03:18,000
En.

81
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:22,260
Five words, and the same trick worked again.

82
00:03:23,360 --> 00:03:25,080
Now a short i.

83
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:30,600
We have three families here, so listen carefully to the ending each time.

84
00:03:31,920 --> 00:03:33,200
First, Ig.

85
00:03:34,320 --> 00:03:34,700
Big.

86
00:03:35,660 --> 00:03:36,180
Pig.

87
00:03:37,160 --> 00:03:37,560
Dig.

88
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:39,320
Wig.

89
00:03:40,560 --> 00:03:40,940
Jig.

90
00:03:42,260 --> 00:03:42,580
Fig.

91
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:44,880
Next, It.

92
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:46,620
Sit.

93
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:48,160
Bit.

94
00:03:49,480 --> 00:03:49,760
Hit.

95
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:51,380
Fit.

96
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:53,000
Kit.

97
00:03:54,440 --> 00:03:54,720
Pit.

98
00:03:56,080 --> 00:03:56,260
Wit.

99
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:58,820
And In.

100
00:04:00,180 --> 00:04:00,440
Pin.

101
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:02,140
Win.

102
00:04:03,340 --> 00:04:03,860
Fin.

103
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:05,600
Tin.

104
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:07,340
Bin.

105
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:09,660
Did you notice something?

106
00:04:10,420 --> 00:04:13,600
All three of those families have the same vowel.

107
00:04:14,260 --> 00:04:16,480
The i sound never changed.

108
00:04:17,060 --> 00:04:19,080
Only the letter at the end did.

109
00:04:19,940 --> 00:04:22,120
That is eighteen more words.

110
00:04:22,900 --> 00:04:24,700
You are reading beautifully.

111
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:27,540
Now a short o.

112
00:04:28,240 --> 00:04:29,580
Three families again.

113
00:04:30,720 --> 00:04:30,960
Og.

114
00:04:31,940 --> 00:04:32,620
Dog.

115
00:04:33,840 --> 00:04:34,300
Log.

116
00:04:35,580 --> 00:04:36,080
Fog.

117
00:04:37,360 --> 00:04:37,940
Hog.

118
00:04:39,200 --> 00:04:39,780
Jog.

119
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:41,200
Ot.

120
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:42,960
Hot.

121
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:44,760
Pot.

122
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:46,660
Dot.

123
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:48,760
Lot.

124
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:50,580
Cot.

125
00:04:52,060 --> 00:04:52,420
Rot.

126
00:04:53,880 --> 00:04:54,240
Got.

127
00:04:55,760 --> 00:04:55,860
Op.

128
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:57,840
Top.

129
00:04:59,440 --> 00:04:59,740
Hop.

130
00:05:01,260 --> 00:05:01,580
Mop.

131
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:03,480
Pop.

132
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:05,240
Cop.

133
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:09,600
Listen to the middle of every one of those words.

134
00:05:10,540 --> 00:05:13,560
It is the same o sound every time.

135
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:17,620
Our last short vowel is u.

136
00:05:18,600 --> 00:05:19,180
Un.

137
00:05:20,380 --> 00:05:20,920
Sun.

138
00:05:22,060 --> 00:05:22,680
Run.

139
00:05:23,900 --> 00:05:24,520
Fun.

140
00:05:26,140 --> 00:05:26,400
Bun.

141
00:05:27,840 --> 00:05:28,380
Gun.

142
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:30,220
Pun.

143
00:05:31,480 --> 00:05:31,860
Ug.

144
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:33,600
Bug.

145
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:35,400
Rug.

146
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:37,240
Hug.

147
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:39,020
Mug.

148
00:05:40,460 --> 00:05:40,840
Dug.

149
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:42,660
Jug.

150
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:47,100
That is twelve more words from two endings.

151
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:56,740
Now I want to show you one more family, but I have to be honest with you about it, because it does not work quite the same way.

152
00:05:57,600 --> 00:05:58,160
Here it is.

153
00:05:59,620 --> 00:05:59,880
All.

154
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:01,720
Ball.

155
00:06:02,980 --> 00:06:03,620
Tall.

156
00:06:04,840 --> 00:06:05,540
Wall.

157
00:06:06,940 --> 00:06:07,560
Fall.

158
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:09,760
Call.

159
00:06:11,140 --> 00:06:11,880
Hall.

160
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:13,980
Mall.

161
00:06:15,360 --> 00:06:16,560
The trick still works.

162
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:19,840
Change the front letter, get a new word.

163
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:22,100
But listen to the middle.

164
00:06:23,560 --> 00:06:23,860
Ball.

165
00:06:24,540 --> 00:06:26,080
That is not a short a.

166
00:06:26,640 --> 00:06:29,840
It does not say the short a sound like Cat.

167
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,720
It has changed into something else.

168
00:06:33,460 --> 00:06:36,880
So we do not sound this family out letter by letter.

169
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:40,380
We learn the whole ending in one piece.

170
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:48,580
When you see those three letters together, a, l, l, you say All.

171
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:50,540
Ball.

172
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:52,360
Tall.

173
00:06:53,520 --> 00:06:54,220
Wall.

174
00:06:55,420 --> 00:06:56,520
Say the ending with me.

175
00:06:57,570 --> 00:06:58,020
All.

176
00:06:59,020 --> 00:07:00,010
And look at the ending.

177
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:01,580
Two l's.

178
00:07:02,240 --> 00:07:03,460
Do you remember why?

179
00:07:04,300 --> 00:07:12,860
That is the Floss rule from Level Five — one clap, short vowel, ends in l, so we double it.

180
00:07:13,820 --> 00:07:18,600
Now it is your turn, and this is exactly what the app will ask you.

181
00:07:19,100 --> 00:07:24,100
I am going to show you a word, and you tell me which letter goes at the front.

182
00:07:25,220 --> 00:07:26,130
Here is the ending.

183
00:07:26,960 --> 00:07:27,580
En.

184
00:07:28,380 --> 00:07:29,940
And here is the picture.

185
00:07:31,060 --> 00:07:31,880
A hen.

186
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:34,180
Which letter starts it?

187
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:37,200
H.

188
00:07:37,940 --> 00:07:38,600
Hen.

189
00:07:39,480 --> 00:07:40,260
That is right!

190
00:07:40,740 --> 00:07:42,080
Let's do one more.

191
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:44,360
The ending is Ug.

192
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:47,440
And the picture is a bug.

193
00:07:48,540 --> 00:07:49,820
Which letter starts it?

194
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:51,920
B.

195
00:07:52,620 --> 00:07:53,280
Bug.

196
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:55,160
Excellent!

197
00:07:55,680 --> 00:07:57,000
That is the whole skill.

198
00:07:57,820 --> 00:08:01,060
Find the ending you know, then work out the front.

199
00:08:02,040 --> 00:08:03,880
Let's say what we learned today.

200
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:08,860
A word family is a group of words that all end the same way.

201
00:08:09,260 --> 00:08:13,760
If you can read the ending, you can read every word in the family.

202
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:16,820
You only have to change the letter at the front.

203
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:23,000
Today you met thirteen families, and you read eighty-one words.

204
00:08:23,920 --> 00:08:24,840
Eighty-one.

205
00:08:25,420 --> 00:08:26,900
From thirteen endings.

206
00:08:27,580 --> 00:08:30,390
That is what makes this trick so useful.

207
00:08:31,820 --> 00:08:33,680
I am really proud of you.

208
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:38,460
This is the skill that turns sounding out into reading.

209
00:08:39,120 --> 00:08:45,840
Next time we will keep going with Level Six and practise these families until they are easy.

210
00:08:46,420 --> 00:08:47,180
Don't miss it!

211
00:08:47,760 --> 00:08:52,250
If you enjoyed this lesson, please like this video and subscribe.

212
00:08:52,820 --> 00:08:56,760
And practise every one of these families in the English Learning app.

213
00:08:57,440 --> 00:09:00,820
It's free on the Apple App Store and Google Play.

214
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:02,180
See you next time!
